To maximize resource utilization on single heterogeneous peer nodes, SwarmLLM's dynamic layer-splitting mechanism automatically partitions model layers between host GPU VRAM and host CPU RAM whenever a model slightly exceeds dedicated VRAM bounds. This dynamic fallback recovers performance to 1.8× over CPU-only execution, preventing unnecessary node disqualification during memory-intensive decoding phases.

Decentralized peer compute execution feeds directly into the unified system threat matrix to guarantee consistent global security enforcement across all participating nodes.

